-- ugcportal-74w.1: a free-text licence grant on a priced listing.
--
-- Generated by `prisma migrate diff --from-migrations prisma/migrations
-- --to-schema prisma/schema.prisma --script`; the comments are the only
-- hand-edit.
--
-- ONE NULLABLE COLUMN, NO DEFAULT, NOTHING BACKFILLED. Every listing that
-- existed before this ran has no per-item grant, which is both the honest
-- state and the one that renders exactly as before: the item page falls back
-- to the site-wide /licence link for NULL. A `DEFAULT ''` would make "no grant
-- was written" and "the grant is the empty string" two rows for one state,
-- which the write path (`recordPrice`, src/lib/curation-price-write.ts)
-- collapses to NULL before it stores anything.
--
-- AN `ADD COLUMN`, NOT A TABLE REBUILD, so it composes with any other bead
-- adding a column to MediaListing (the reasoning 20261010100000 gives for
-- ResaleRightsReview). The length bound and the Instagram refusal are in the
-- writer (src/lib/licence-terms.ts), not a CHECK constraint here, for the same
-- reason priceCents' bounds are: the writer is the only path to the column,
-- and a refusal has to reach the admin as a sentence, not as a driver error.
--
-- DEPLOY ORDER: apply before the new build. A new build against an
-- un-migrated database fails every MediaListing read (the generated client
-- selects every scalar column), which is the failure scripts/check-migrations.mjs
-- exists to catch locally; an old build against a migrated database ignores
-- the column.

-- AlterTable
ALTER TABLE "MediaListing" ADD COLUMN "licenceTerms" TEXT;
